      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\n`docs/design/cuda_graphs_multimodal.md` maintains the support matrix for multimodal encoder CUDA graphs. \r\n\r\nGLM-5.3-Flash (`Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration`) already supports them on main — it inherits the full `SupportsEncoderCudaGraph` implementation from `Glm4vForConditionalGeneration` — but is missing from the matrix. \r\n\r\nThis PR adds the row (image ✅ / video ✅); no code changes.\r\n\r\nDuplicate-work check (per AGENTS.md): no open PR covers GLM-5.3-Flash in this matrix. No new CI test: the capability is inherited, not new code, and the shared parent implementation already carries coverage; same reasoning as the docs-only precedent in #44720.\r\n\r\n## Commands\r\n\r\n- Server (stock main @ v0.32.0, 8×H200):\r\n\r\n  ```bash\r\n  vllm serve /models/GLM-5.3-Flash --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\\r\n    --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mm_encoder\": true}'\r\n  ```\r\n\r\n- Image request: OpenAI chat completion with a base64 PNG (448×448 solid blue), `max_tokens: 64`\r\n- Video request: OpenAI chat completion with a base64 MP4 (4 frames solid red), `max_tokens: 200`\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n- Startup log (all 8 TP ranks): `Encoder CUDA graph capture complete. Captured 8 graphs across 1 paths.`\r\n- Image request: HTTP 200 — `The image appears to be entirely blue - a solid blue color throughout...` (usage: prompt 281, completion 43)\r\n- Video request: HTTP 200 — `...Frame 00:00 is solid red...Red` (usage: prompt 55, completion 68)\r\n- No ERROR / Traceback in the server log during either request.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
